<section id="Pt1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part"><span id="Pt1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center">Appendix</span>
<br class="ltx_break"></h2>

<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Derivation of the Dual-form Solutions</h3>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first prove the equivalence between the primal and dual forms of ridge regression (Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 Efficient Dual-form Solution ‣ 3 Joint Sequence Compression via Test-time Regression ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>). We then show that, with learnable diagonal regularization, rescaling the keys yields the dual solution in Eq. <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Efficient Dual-form Solution ‣ 3 Joint Sequence Compression via Test-time Regression ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Equivalence of the Primal and Dual Forms.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Push-through identity)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})^{-1}\bm{K}^{\top}=\bm{K}^{\top}(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})^{-1}\bm{K}^{\top}=\bm{K}^{\top}(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> are positive semidefinite. Hence, for <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrices <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are symmetric positive definite and therefore invertible. Expanding both sides directly gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})\,\bm{K}^{\top}=\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{K}^{\top}=\bm{K}^{\top}(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})\,\bm{K}^{\top}=\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{K}^{\top}=\bm{K}^{\top}(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Left-multiplying by <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and right-multiplying by <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> yields Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Lemma 1 (Push-through identity). ‣ Appendix A Derivation of the Dual-form Solutions ‣ Appendix ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Right-multiplying Eq. <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Lemma 1 (Push-through identity). ‣ Appendix A Derivation of the Dual-form Solutions ‣ Appendix ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> by <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}</annotation></semantics></math> turns the primal solution in Eq. <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.2 Constructing the Regression Problem ‣ 3 Joint Sequence Compression via Test-time Regression ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> into the dual form in Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 Efficient Dual-form Solution ‣ 3 Joint Sequence Compression via Test-time Regression ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}^{\star}=(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})^{-1}\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{v}=\bm{K}^{\top}(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}\bm{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑲</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}^{\star}=(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\lambda\bm{I}_{d})^{-1}\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{v}=\bm{K}^{\top}(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}\bm{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the row space of <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Its dual coefficients <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\alpha}=(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}\bm{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\alpha}=(\bm{K}\bm{K}^{\top}+\lambda\bm{I}_{T})^{-1}\bm{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are obtained by solving a single <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\times T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\times T</annotation></semantics></math> system.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dual Solution under Diagonal Regularization.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}=\operatorname{diag}(\delta_{1},\ldots,\delta_{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}=\operatorname{diag}(\delta_{1},\ldots,\delta_{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{j}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{j}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widetilde{\bm{K}}=\bm{K}\bm{D}^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>𝐃</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\bm{K}}=\bm{K}\bm{D}^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the solution of Eq. <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2 Constructing the Regression Problem ‣ 3 Joint Sequence Compression via Test-time Regression ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\bm{D})^{-1}\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{v}=\bm{D}^{-1/2}\widetilde{\bm{K}}^{\top}\big(\bm{I}_{T}+\widetilde{\bm{K}}\widetilde{\bm{K}}^{\top}\big)^{-1}\bm{v}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝑫</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{K}+\bm{D})^{-1}\bm{K}^{\top}\bm{v}=\bm{D}^{-1/2}\widetilde{\bm{K}}^{\top}\big(\bm{I}_{T}+\widetilde{\bm{K}}\widetilde{\bm{K}}^{\top}\big)^{-1}\bm{v}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
