<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Ablation on the Value Parameterization</h4>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> compression setup, we compare five parameterizations of <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: (i) <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">constant</em> (<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math>); (ii) <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">linear</em> (<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\bm{a}^{\top}\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\bm{a}^{\top}\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>); (iii) <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MLP</em> (<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\mathrm{MLP}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\mathrm{MLP}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>); (iv) <em id="A5.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bilinear</em> (<math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\mathrm{MLP}(\bm{x}_{t})^{\top}\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>MLP</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\mathrm{MLP}(\bm{x}_{t})^{\top}\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>); and (v) their convolutional variants using local <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> features <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Conv}(\bm{X})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Conv</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Conv}(\bm{X})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ E.2 Ablation on the Value Parameterization ‣ Appendix E Additional Experimental Results ‣ Appendix ‣ Rethinking Sequence Compression withTest-time Regression" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we observe:
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(1) Content dependence is critical</span>: The constant target yields the lowest average (53.56), while the linear target gains <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.74" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.74</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.74</annotation></semantics></math>, showing that regression targets must encode token content to form effective summaries.
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(2) Deeper heads offer marginal gains</span>: Plain MLP matches the linear baseline (54.30), and adding convolution degrades it (53.91). Although the bilinear head slightly improves performance (54.55), its convolutional counterpart sees no further gain (54.37).
<span id="A5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(3) Spatial context outweighs head capacity</span>: Combining local convolution with a linear readout, <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}=\bm{a}^{\top}\mathrm{Conv}(\bm{X})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Conv</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}=\bm{a}^{\top}\mathrm{Conv}(\bm{X})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, achieves the best overall score (54.85).
These results indicate that value capacity is not the bottleneck; local neighborhood aggregation provides a more effective inductive bias than non-linear projection.</p>
</div>
